BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Emory Cosmos Datathon 2026
DTSTART:20260804T130000Z
DTEND:20260805T210000Z
DTSTAMP:20260731T203835Z
UID:winship-6728@seminar-calendar
DESCRIPTION:Event type: Lectures and Training\n\nJoin the Emory Health Ser
 vices Research Center for the Emory Cosmos Datathon 2026 on Tuesday\, Augu
 st 4 and Wednesday\, August 5. The event brings together clinicians\, rese
 archers\, data scientists\, analysts and trainees to explore innovative re
 search using Epic Cosmos\, one of the largest de-identified electronic hea
 lth record (EHR) databases in the world\, with over 300 million patient re
 cords. Participants will work collaboratively to explore real-world health
  data\, address pressing clinical and health services research question\, 
 and develop impactful projects. Teams will receive guidance from clinical 
 subject-matter experts and Epic staff while investigating topics such as q
 uality and patient safety\, clinical operations\, cost-effectiveness and c
 linical outcomes. Participating teams will have the opportunity to compete
  for an Emory Health Services Research Center-funded award\, which will su
 pport the advancement of their projects toward publication\, conference pr
 esentation or a larger grant submission. Register today Note: Non-Cosmos u
 sers are welcome to attend the educational sessions the morning of August 
 4\, and the team presentations and award announcement the afternoon of Aug
 ust 5.\n\nWinship event page: https://apps.winshipcancer.emory.edu/admin/E
 vent/6728/emory-cosmos-datathon-2026/
LOCATION:CNR 1000\, Claudia Nance Rollins Building Rollins School of Publi
 c Health 1518 Clifton Road NE Atlanta \, Georgia 30322
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
URL:https://apps.winshipcancer.emory.edu/admin/Event/6728/emory-cosmos-dat
 athon-2026/
END:VEVENT
