BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:In Person - 2026 Winship Cell and Molecular Biology (CMB) Research
  Program Retreat - "Emerging Frontiers in Cancer Biology: New Mechanisms\,
  Innovative Technologies\, and Translational Team Science"
DTSTART:20260814T123000Z
DTEND:20260814T183000Z
DTSTAMP:20260731T203835Z
UID:winship-6619@seminar-calendar
DESCRIPTION:Presenter: Joseph Castello\, PhD Professor\, Neurological Surg
 ery University of California San Francisco\n\nEvent type: Retreat\n\nJoin 
 us for the 2026 Winship Cancer Institute Cell and Molecular Biology (CMB) 
 Research Program Retreat\, Emerging Frontiers in Cancer Biology: New Mecha
 nisms\, Innovative Technologies\, and Translational Team Science. We invit
 e you to take part in a day of collaboration\, discovery\, and forward‑t
 hinking discussion as we explore cutting‑edge biological mechanisms\, hi
 ghlight innovative technologies shaping the future of cancer research\, an
 d strengthen the team‑science approaches that drive meaningful translati
 onal impact. Program Highlights Keynote Presentation: "Immortality and Evo
 lution: Partners in the Cancer Crime" Joe Costello\, PhD Professor and Kar
 en Osney Brownstein Endowed Chair in Molecular Neuro-Oncology Department o
 f Neurological Surgery University of California San Francisco Scientific D
 irector\, UCSF Brain Tumor Center Program Director\, UCSF Brain Tumor SPOR
 E The event will also feature faculty presentations\, COE updates\, lunch 
 breakout sessions\, and a panel discussion. Breakfast and lunch will be pr
 ovided. Schedule Date: Friday\, August 14\, 2026 8:30 a.m. Breakfast & Net
 working 9:00 a.m. Welcome and Program Updates 9:15 a.m. – 11:30 a.m. | S
 cientific Talks 11:30 a.m. – 12:30 p.m. | Keynote Presentation 12:30 p.m
 . – 1:20 p.m. | Lunch and Breakout Discussion Sessions 1:20 p.m. – 2:3
 0 p.m. | Scientific Talks and Closing Remarks\n\nWinship event page: https
 ://apps.winshipcancer.emory.edu/admin/Event/6619/in-person---2026-winship-
 cell-and-molecular-biology-cmb-research-program-retreat---emerging-frontie
 rs-in-cancer-biology-new-mechanisms-innovative-technologies-and-translatio
 nal-team-science/
LOCATION:John H. Kauffman Auditorium (C5012\, 5th Floor Winship) Winship C
 ancer Institute 1365 Clifton Road NE\, Building C Atlanta \, Georgia 30322
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
URL:https://apps.winshipcancer.emory.edu/admin/Event/6619/in-person---2026
 -winship-cell-and-molecular-biology-cmb-research-program-retreat---emergin
