BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:17th Annual Winship Oncology Nursing Symposium
DTSTART:20260821T230000Z
DTEND:20260822T203000Z
DTSTAMP:20260731T203835Z
UID:winship-6697@seminar-calendar
DESCRIPTION:Event type: Lectures and Training\n\nOverview Join us for the 
 17th Annual Winship Oncology Nursing Symposium at the Crowne Plaza Atlanta
  Perimeter at Ravinia\, Friday\, August 21 - Saturday\, August 22\, 2026. 
 Conference Highlights Theme: Caring Beyond the Cure: Advancing Oncology Nu
 rsing Across the Cancer Continuum Attendees will benefit from an intimate 
 learning environment and the opportunity to meet and learn from local\, na
 tional and internationally recognized oncology leaders. Presentations and 
 breakout sessions will explore current research and trends in oncology nur
 sing practice. Participants will gain insight and strategies to translate 
 evidence-based learning into clinical practice. Friday Night Fun: Begin th
 e 17th Annual Winship Oncology Nursing Symposium with a lively kickoff eve
 nt featuring disco bingo and a friendly 70s costume contest. Step out in y
 our go-go boots and connect with colleagues during an evening of laughter\
 , networking\, food\, and exciting giveaways. This signature event sets th
 e tone for a dynamic symposium experience\, building energy and connection
  that will carry through a weekend of learning\, collaboration\, and profe
 ssional growth. Keynote Speaker Renee Thompson\, DNP\, RN\, FAONL\, FAAN\,
  CSP® Chief Executive Officer & Founder\, Healthy Workforce Institute Dr.
  Renee Thompson is the CEO & Founder of the Healthy Workforce Institute \,
  working with healthcare leaders to cultivate a professional workforce by 
 addressing bullying and incivility. Renee is a bestselling author\, hosts 
 a popular podcast\, and is one of only 30 nurses worldwide to hold the pre
 stigious Certified Speaking Professional designation. In 2018\, she was re
 cognized as one of LinkedIn’s Top 10 Voices in Healthcare for her contri
 butions to the global online healthcare community. In 2022 and 2023\, she 
 was identified as one of LinkedIn's top 5 Nurse Influencers. In 2022\, Ren
 ee was inducted as a Fellow of the American Academy of Nursing for her wor
 k to eradicate disruptive behaviors in healthcare and In March 2026\, Rene
 e was inducted as a Fellow of the American Organization for Nursing Leader
 ship for her sustained contributions to the specialty of nursing leadershi
 p\, commitment to service and influence in shaping health care by addressi
 ng disruptive behaviors. Hotel A block of rooms has been reserved for conf
 erence attendees at the Crowne Plaza Atlanta Perimeter at Ravinia at the d
 iscounted rate of $139 per night. Rooms are available on a first come\, fi
 rst served basis\, with a cut-off date of July 31. Call to book your room:
  (770) 395-7700\n\nWinship event page: https://apps.winshipcancer.emory.ed
 u/admin/Event/6697/17th-annual-winship-oncology-nursing-symposium/
LOCATION:Crowne Plaza: Atlanta Perimeter at Ravinia 4355 Ashford Dunwoody 
 Road Atlanta \, Georgia 30346
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
URL:https://apps.winshipcancer.emory.edu/admin/Event/6697/17th-annual-wins
 hip-oncology-nursing-symposium/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:In Person - Discovery and Developmental Therapeutics (DDT) and Can
 cer Immunology (CI) Joint Program Retreat - "Breaking Immune Barriers: Tra
 nslating Discovery into Tomorrow’s Therapies"
DTSTART:20260825T120000Z
DTEND:20260825T200000Z
DTSTAMP:20260731T203835Z
UID:winship-6698@seminar-calendar
DESCRIPTION:Event type: Retreat\n\nJoin us for the Discovery and Developme
 ntal Therapeutics (DDT) and Cancer Immunology (CI) Joint Retreat\, “Brea
 king Immune Barriers: Translating Discovery into Tomorrow’s Therapies.
 ” We invite you to take part in a day of collaboration\, insight and for
 ward‑thinking discussion as we explore innovative research and chart the
  path from immune‑focused discovery to transformative therapies of the f
 uture. Program Highlights Keynote Presentation: "Second Wave Modern Immuno
 therapy Drug Development in Solid Tumors" Ryan Sullivan\, MD Director\, Cu
 taneous Medical Oncology Program\; Associate Professor Mass General Brigha
