BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:2026 Cancer Biology T32 Training Program Retreat
DTSTART:20260827T131500Z
DTEND:20260827T180000Z
DTSTAMP:20260731T203835Z
UID:winship-6752@seminar-calendar
DESCRIPTION:Event type: Retreat\n\nPlease join us for the 3rd annual Cance
 r Biology T32 Training Program Retreat! The NIH T32 training grant support
 s both pre-doctoral and post-doctoral trainees within Winship\, promoting 
 innovative and exciting research within multiple laboratories. This event 
 will feature keynote speaker Melinda Bachini\, chief patient officer of th
 e Cholangiocarcinoma Foundation\, in addition to talks from trainees suppo
 rted by this grant. We are excited to showcase all our trainees' exciting 
 work and hope to see you there! RSVP HERE by August 24 Schedule 9:15 a.m. 
 Check-in\, coffee and refreshments 9:30 a.m. Welcome Message and Introduct
 ion of Keynote Speaker David Yu\, MD\, PhD\, director\, Post-doctoral Trai
 ning Program Sumin Kang\, PhD\, and Gregory Lesinski\, PhD\, MPH\, directo
 rs\, Pre-doctoral Training Program 9:45 a.m. Keynote Address – "Outlier:
  The Patient Behind the Data" Melinda Bachini\, chief patient officer\, Ch
 olangiocarcinoma Foundation 10:45 a.m. Break 11:00 a.m. Post-doctoral Trai
 nee Talks Adedeji Adebayo\, DVM\, PhD\, MS\, Lisa Nieland\, PhD\, MS\, Chr
 istina Ramelow\, PhD\, MS\, and Nolan Tucker\, PhD 12:00 p.m. Lunch (provi
 ded) 1:00 p.m. Pre-doctoral Trainee Talks Anna Baj\, Alexis Dixon\, Ruby F
 reeman and Chloe Hope 2:00 p.m. Closing Remarks Alexis Dixon\n\nWinship ev
 ent page: https://apps.winshipcancer.emory.edu/admin/Event/6752/2026-cance
 r-biology-t32-training-program-retreat/
LOCATION:John H. Kauffman Auditorium (C5012\, 5th Floor Winship) Winship C
 ancer Institute 1365 Clifton Road NE\, Building C Atlanta \, Georgia 30322
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
URL:https://apps.winshipcancer.emory.edu/admin/Event/6752/2026-cancer-biol
 ogy-t32-training-program-retreat/
END:VEVENT
