BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Cure to Cancer Survivorship: A New Era of Biomarkers\, Interventio
 ns\, and Care Models
DTSTART:20270206T170000Z
DTEND:20270206T180000Z
DTSTAMP:20260731T203835Z
UID:winship-6760@seminar-calendar
DESCRIPTION:Event type: Lectures and Training\n\nOverview Cure to Cancer S
 urvivorship: A New Era of Biomarkers\, Interventions\, and Care Models is 
 a one-day educational conference jointly sponsored by Winship Cancer Insti
 tute of Emory University and Physicians’ Education Resource (PER®). Can
 cer survivorship is one of the most rapidly evolving areas in oncology. As
  treatment efficacy improves across many tumor types\, the long-term physi
 cal\, psychological\, and social impact of cancer management has emerged a
 s an important topic as part of overall cancer care. This inaugural progra
 m for oncologists and other health care professionals managing cancer feat
 ures expert speakers addressing cancer survivorship topics from screening 
 through diagnosis\, treatment\, and long-term follow-up. Key program featu
 res will include expert presentations and holistic discussions on how to i
 ntegrate survivorship into clinical decision-making from the time of diagn
 osis\, dose delivery\, and adherence optimization through lifestyle and su
 pportive interventions. Management of chronic debilitating toxicities\, su
 ch as fatigue and nausea\, and discussion of long-term efficacy and safety
  data for key therapies and extended treatment regimens will also be revie
 wed. Specific topics will include: Treatment selection\, balancing long-te
 rm efficacy with long-term safety and patient-reported outcomes Supportive
  physical care during and after treatment Long-term adherence in the setti
 ng of extended medical therapies: behavioral strategies\, lifestyle advice
 \, technology-enabled tools\, and shared decision-making frameworks Target
  Audience This educational activity is directed toward academic and commun
 ity-based oncologists\, hematologists\, transplant physicians\, nurse prac
 titioners (NPs)\, physician assistants (PAs)\, nurses\, and other health c
 are professionals involved in the management of patients with cancer. Prog
 ram Chair Neil M. Iyengar\, MD Register Today\n\nWinship event page: https
 ://apps.winshipcancer.emory.edu/admin/Event/6760/cure-to-cancer-survivorsh
 ip-a-new-era-of-biomarkers-interventions-and-care-models/
LOCATION:Loews Atlanta Hotel 1065 Peachtree Street NE Atlanta \, Georgia 3
 0309
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
URL:https://apps.winshipcancer.emory.edu/admin/Event/6760/cure-to-cancer-s
 urvivorship-a-new-era-of-biomarkers-interventions-and-care-models/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:2027 Georgia Cancer Summit
DTSTART:20270209T130000Z
DTEND:20270209T200000Z
DTSTAMP:20260731T203835Z
UID:winship-6758@seminar-calendar
DESCRIPTION:Event type: Lectures and Training\n\n2027 Georgia Cancer Summi
 t Transforming Cancer Control: Rural Equity in Action The Georgia Cancer S
 ummit is co-hosted by Winship Cancer Institute of Emory University\, Georg
 ia CORE\, the Georgia Department of Public Health\, the American Cancer So
 ciety\, and the Georgia Cancer Control Consortium. Purpose The goal of the
  2027 Georgia Cancer Summit is to catalyze efforts to reduce barriers to a
 ccess to prevention\, screening and quality cancer care for all Georgians.
  Summit participants will: Learn best practices to advance cancer preventi
 on\, control\, and research throughout Georgia Enhance understanding of sp
 ecial challenges for cancer prevention & control among rural populations H
 ear about challenges in the current government funding environment and lea
 rn best practices to establish partnerships and take action at the local a
 nd state levels Be able to network with other organizations that may lead 
 to new partnerships Identify ways your organization can get more involved 
 in advancing Georgia’s comprehensive cancer control objectives Audience 
 The Georgia Cancer Summit is for public health professionals\, health care
  providers\, health advocates\, researchers\, community-based organization
 s\, and others committed to improving cancer health equity in Georgia thro
 ugh cancer prevention and control and community-engaged research.\n\nWinsh
 ip event page: https://apps.winshipcancer.emory.edu/admin/Event/6758/2027-
 georgia-cancer-summit/
LOCATION:University of Georgia Tifton Campus Conference Center 15 R D C Rd
  Tifton \, Georgia 31794
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
URL:https://apps.winshipcancer.emory.edu/admin/Event/6758/2027-georgia-can
 cer-summit/
END:VEVENT
